\title{Even and odd}
\date{2026-04-08T13:50:14Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Note that we can finally use the [Division Algorithm](00DD) to tidy up our notions of even and odd. We [defined being even](004V) as #{\Even(n) \equiv \ext{k}{\Z}{n = 2k}} and [we defined being odd](004W) as #{\Odd(n) \equiv \ext{k}{\Z}{n = 2k+1}}.  Intuitively, we know that if a number is not even, then it has to be odd, and vice versa, but we haven't proved that until now.}

\transclude{00DO}   % Theorem: even \/ odd
\transclude{00DQ}   % not Even <-> Odd etc
